        "principal_competence"
      ],
      "mechanisms": [
        "decision_cost"
      ],
      "prediction": "vanishes",
      "rationale": "On this reading decision_cost is the sole convex term that gives A its curvature, and both observed effects are that term seen from two directions: alpha reduces what must be deliberated, and principal_competence proxies the difficulty of deliberating it. Removing decision_cost should therefore flatten A entirely with respect to both. This is the least likely of the four accounts, because decision_cost is described as a burden on the central authority as a function of breadth of enfranchisement, and neither alpha nor principal_competence is obviously that breadth; but it is not impossible if breadth is itself a function of the split alpha governs."
